WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.050
AI coding agents write code fast —

2
00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:06.780
and they happily report done on things nobody checked.

3
00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:10.220
That's how prototypes end up in production.

4
00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:15.660
Every service I ship runs under this quality contour:

5
00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:18.860
a catalog of twenty-two automatic checks.

6
00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:21.470
Here it runs on this very site.

7
00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:26.750
Each check reports how much it actually looked at —

8
00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:32.270
because no problems found means nothing if it saw no code.

9
00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:36.270
Now I break one on purpose:

10
00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:40.100
a five-hundred-line limit becomes fifty thousand.

11
00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:41.630
It still passes —

12
00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:45.310
and still calls itself a five-hundred-line check.

13
00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:50.710
This is the doctor.

14
00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:54.380
It plants a known mistake in front of every check.

15
00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:59.590
A check that stays silent isn't just weak — it's lying.

16
00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:03.360
It even noticed that the check itself was edited.

17
00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:05.940
And a lie fails the whole run.

18
00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:10.290
Put the line back, and the lie is gone.

19
00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:14.440
The contour also limits itself:

20
00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:17.700
the number of checks is capped at twenty-two,

21
00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:20.080
so it can't quietly bloat.

22
00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:24.110
It runs in eight repositories.

23
00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:27.570
Every problem it missed is logged —

24
00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:30.570
and each new one has to name the check

25
00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:32.250
that should have caught it.

26
00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:36.810
That's how two services went from a bare spec

27
00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:39.900
to production in under three weeks —

28
00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:42.330
checked like a corporate product.

29
00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:46.670
Nothing counts as done unless a mechanism can refuse it.
